<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabriel Narutowicz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabriel Narutowicz was a Polish engineer and politician who became the first president of the Second Polish Republic in December 1922. A professor of hydraulic engineering in Zurich, he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> after independence and served as a minister. Elected by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> with the votes of the left and the national minorities, he was shot dead by a right-wing nationalist at an art exhibition in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> five days after taking office.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gabriel-narutowicz.jpg" alt="Gabriel Narutowicz" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (From ETH Zurich) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_Narutowicz_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
